[V:1] E2 E E | F2 E2 | A G F F | E4 |
w: 1.~Spir- it of God, de- scend up- on my heart;
w: 2.~I ask no dream, no proph- et ec- sta- sies,
w: 3.~Hast Thou not bid me love Thee, God and King?
w: 4.~Teach me to feel that Thou art al- ways nigh;
w: 5.~Teach me to love Thee as Thine an- gels love,
[V:1] c2 B A | G2 A2 | B G A A | G4 |
w: Wean it from earth; through all its puls- es move.
w: No sud- den rend- ing of the veil of clay,
w: All, all Thine own, soul, heart and strength and mind.
w: Teach me the strug- gles of the soul to bear,
w: One ho- ly pas- sion fill- ing all my frame;
[V:1] G2 G G | B2 A2 | F A B c | d4 |
w: Stoop to my weak- ness, might- y as Thou art,
w: No an- gel vis- it- ant, no o- pening skies;
w: I see Thy cross— there teach my heart to cling:
w: To check the ris- ing doubt, the reb- el sigh;
w: The bap- tism of the heaven de- scend- ed Dove,
[V:1] e2 d c | B A G c | G2 F2 | G4 |]
w: And make me love Thee as I ought to love.
w: But take the dim- ness of my soul a- way.
w: O let me seek Thee, and, O let me find!
w: Teach me the pa- tience of un- an- swered prayer.
w: My heart an al- tar, and Thy love the flame.
